
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<style>
    .privacy-page {
        padding: 45px 0 65px;
        background: #f7faf8;
        min-height: 75vh;
    }

    .privacy-header {
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #183d2b, #2d6547);
        color: #fff;
        padding: 48px 35px;
        border-radius: 18px;
        margin-bottom: 30px;
        box-shadow: 0 8px 25px rgba(25, 60, 42, .12);
    }

    .privacy-header h1 {
        font-size: 34px;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .privacy-header p {
        margin: 0;
        color: #e1eee5;
        font-size: 15px;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .privacy-content {
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid #e5ece7;
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 32px;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 18px rgba(25, 60, 42, .04);
    }

    .privacy-section {
        padding: 22px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #edf1ee;
    }

    .privacy-section:first-child {
        padding-top: 0;
    }

    .privacy-section:last-child {
        border-bottom: none;
        padding-bottom: 0;
    }

    .privacy-section h3 {
        color: #23372b;
        font-size: 19px;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .privacy-section p,
    .privacy-section li {
        color: #647168;
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.85;
    }

    .privacy-section ul {
        padding-left: 22px;
        margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .privacy-note {
        background: #f0f6f1;
        border-left: 4px solid #34744d;
        padding: 17px 20px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin-top: 25px;
        color: #405849;
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .privacy-icon {
        display: inline-flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        width: 38px;
        height: 38px;
        background: #edf5ef;
        color: #34744d;
        border-radius: 10px;
        margin-right: 10px;
        font-size: 17px;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 768px) {
        .privacy-page {
            padding: 25px 0 40px;
        }

        .privacy-header {
            padding: 32px 23px;
        }

        .privacy-header h1 {
            font-size: 27px;
        }

        .privacy-content {
            padding: 22px;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="privacy-page">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="privacy-header">
            <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p>
                Your privacy matters to us. This page explains how the
                University Library Management System handles information
                related to student accounts and library activities.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-content">

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">01</span>
                    Introduction
                </h3>
                <p>
                    The University Library Management System (ULMS) is
                    designed to support library services within the
                    University of Lahore. This Privacy Policy explains
                    what information is handled by the system and how
                    it is used for library management purposes.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">02</span>
                    Information We Collect
                </h3>
                <p>
                    To provide library services, ULMS may store and
                    process the following information:
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Student name and university email address.</li>
                    <li>Student account and profile information.</li>
                    <li>Book borrowing and return records.</li>
                    <li>Book issue dates, due dates and return dates.</li>
                    <li>Account and access information required to operate the system.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">03</span>
                    Google Authentication
                </h3>
                <p>
                    Student access is intended for eligible University
                    of Lahore accounts through Google authentication.
                    The system uses the authenticated account information
                    to identify the student and associate it with the
                    relevant student profile.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Students should use their eligible university email
                    account when accessing the system.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">04</span>
                    Student Accounts and Profiles
                </h3>
                <p>
                    Student profile information is used to identify
                    students and provide access to their library
                    services. Account information may be associated
                    with borrowing records so that library activities
                    can be managed accurately.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">05</span>
                    Library Borrowing Records
                </h3>
                <p>
                    ULMS maintains records of books issued to students,
                    including the relevant book copy, issue date,
                    due date and return information.
                </p>
                <p>
                    These records help authorized library staff manage
                    book availability, monitor active loans and maintain
                    borrowing history.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">06</span>
                    Information Access and Security
                </h3>
                <p>
                    Access to library information is based on the
                    permissions assigned to different system roles.
                    Students, library staff and administrators have
                    different levels of access according to their
                    responsibilities.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Users should keep their university accounts secure
                    and should not share their login credentials with
                    others.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">07</span>
                    Use of Information
                </h3>
                <p>
                    Information handled by ULMS is intended to support
                    university library operations, including student
                    identification, book issuing, book returns,
                    borrowing history and library administration.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-section">
                <h3>
                    <span class="privacy-icon">08</span>
                    Contact Information
                </h3>
                <p>
                    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or
                    the handling of information within ULMS, please
                    contact the relevant University Library
                    Administration.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="privacy-note">
                <strong>Important:</strong>
                This policy describes the intended use of information
                within ULMS. It should be reviewed and approved by the
                University Library Administration before the system
                is published for official use.
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
